meta {
  name: Delete Family Attribute Link
  type: http
  seq: 10
}

delete {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-families/REPLACE_WITH_FAMILY_ID/attributes/REPLACE_WITH_ATTRIBUTE_ID
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-15 against the disposable scratch product family
  from "Create Family Attribute Link.bru" (id `6aa97212a30ca5945169a21e`)
  and the Phase 1 kept text-attribute fixture (id
  `6a9f1bf72b6fd055ffb7c7e1`) on "David's Dev Account". Brand-new
  endpoint in the 2026-09-15 `openapi_pimv3.json` refresh -- unlinks an
  attribute from a family without deleting the attribute itself (the
  Phase 1 `wc_test_text` fixture was left fully intact afterward,
  confirmed via a follow-up `GET /product-attributes/{id}`).

  ## What it does
  `DELETE /product-families/{id}/attributes/{attribute_id}` -- `204 No
  Content`. A follow-up `GET` on the same pair then returns `404` with an
  error shape that names both ids explicitly (more specific than the
  generic "Document with id ... not found" seen elsewhere):
  `{"errors":[{"name":"NotFoundError","description":"Association
  (product_family_id=..., attribute_id=...) not found"}]}`.

  ## Also confirmed: the identity endpoint's POST verb
  `openapi_pimv3.json` also declares `POST` on this same identity path
  (`/product-families/{id}/attributes/{attribute_id}`), alongside the
  collection-level `POST /product-families/{id}/attributes` used in
  "Create Family Attribute Link.bru". Tested it against an already-linked
  attribute: it behaves as an idempotent link-by-URL variant, not a
  distinct action -- `409 {"errors":[{"name":"AlreadyExists","description":
  "Attribute <id> is already linked to this product family."}]}` when the
  link already exists (confirmed both with and without a body). Likely
  the same effect as the collection POST but taking `attribute_id` from
  the URL instead of the body; a link to a *not-yet-linked* attribute via
  this route wasn't separately captured this session, but the 409 shape
  itself is a real, useful finding for docs (idempotent-create semantics).
}

example {
  name: Delete Family Attribute Link - Success (204, then 404 on follow-up GET)
  description: Real response captured 2026-09-15.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-families/6aa97212a30ca5945169a21e/attributes/6a9f1bf72b6fd055ffb7c7e1
    method: delete
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 204
      text: No Content
    }
    headers: {
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        (empty body)
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: Get Family Attribute by ID - After Delete (404, Association Not Found)
  description: Real response captured 2026-09-15, follow-up GET immediately after the DELETE above -- note the more specific "Association (...) not found" error shape.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-families/6aa97212a30ca5945169a21e/attributes/6a9f1bf72b6fd055ffb7c7e1
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 404
      text: Not Found
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [],
          "errors": [
            {
              "name": "NotFoundError",
              "description": "Association (product_family_id=6aa97212a30ca5945169a21e, attribute_id=6a9f1bf72b6fd055ffb7c7e1) not found"
            }
          ]
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: Link Family Attribute via Identity POST - Already Linked (409)
  description: Real response captured 2026-09-15 against a second disposable scratch family ("WC Test Product Family 2", id `6aa9727aa30ca5945169a226`, since deleted) -- confirms the identity endpoint's POST verb is an idempotent link, not a distinct action.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-families/6aa9727aa30ca5945169a226/attributes/6a9f1bf72b6fd055ffb7c7e1
    method: post
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {}
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 409
      text: Conflict
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [],
          "errors": [
            {
              "name": "AlreadyExists",
              "description": "Attribute 6a9f1bf72b6fd055ffb7c7e1 is already linked to this product family."
            }
          ]
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}
